{"id":"m7-scr-05","category":"routine","note":"MyChart message thread as seen in Epic In Basket.","htmls":["<html><body style='margin:0;font-family:DejaVu Sans,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;color:#222;background:#fff'><div style='background:#f3f3f3;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px 12px'><div style='font-size:14px'><b>Park, Seo-yeon</b> (F, 39 y.o.) &nbsp; MRN 2208561 &nbsp; DOB 08/19/1987</div><div style='color:#555'>Subject: Question before Friday infusion</div></div><div style='padding:10px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e5e5'><div style='color:#555;margin-bottom:4px'>From patient - 11/02/2026 7:48 PM</div><div>Hi, I have had a low grade fever (100.6) since last night and some mouth sores. I am scheduled for cycle 3 of AC on Friday 11/06/2026. Should I still come in? My husband Min-jun can drive me either way. Best number is 555-0163 or email seoyeon.park88@mailbox.example.com. Thank you.</div></div><div style='padding:10px 12px'><div style='color:#555;margin-bottom:4px'>Reply - Infusion RN - 11/03/2026 8:15 AM</div><div>Thank you for letting us know. Please check your temperature again this evening; if it reaches 100.4 or higher call the oncology line right away. For the mouth sores, start the salt and baking soda rinses 4 times daily. We will draw a CBC Friday morning before deciding on treatment. We have added a note to your chart.</div></div></body></html>"],"phi":["Park, Seo-yeon","2208561","08/19/1987","11/02/2026","11/06/2026","Min-jun","555-0163","seoyeon.park88@mailbox.example.com","11/03/2026"],"keep":["low grade fever (100.6)","cycle 3 of AC","salt and baking soda rinses 4 times daily"]},
